3. Conceptual Question Answer: Hot Reload vs. Hot Restart
Hot Reload
Mechanism: Injects updated source code files into the running Dart Virtual Machine (VM) without rebuilding the app binary or destroying the current application state.
When to Use: Ideal for UI tweaks, styling adjustments, building new layouts, or fixing minor bugs inside widget build methods where preserving the active application state (e.g., form inputs, navigation stack, counter values) is preferred.
Hot Restart
Mechanism: Destroys the current app state, resets the Dart VM, and re-executes the application from the main() entry point.
When to Use: Required when modifying application state initialization, changing global variables, updating initState() methods, modifying asset declarations in pubspec.yaml, or implementing major architectural changes that static injection cannot apply dynamically.
